    "translation": "I’ll add some background information: you don’t come to a colonoscopy unprepared. Seeing as this is an exam that explores the final and largest part of the intestine – that is, the colon – it’s critical to dedicate a few days to a process that allows you to empty and cleanse it as thoroughly as possible of what passes through it during daily functioning, namely feces in various stages of digestion and elimination. To arrive clear for the exam, you follow a diet strictly free of fiber and other slow-moving foods, fast for twenty-four hours beforehand, and undergo a laxative procedure consisting of a bowel lavage performed by drinking four liters of a sodium salt solution that completely empties and cleanses the bowel: like a great flood that washes away everything that normally passes through our guts. I had done it all with great care."
