    "translation": "After all, I muse, our bodies are, phylogenetically speaking, coiled-up worms in our abdomens and chests, equipped with exoskeletons that allow them to interact with the world through their limbs. Obviously, I know that, with regard to the body, ours would be an endoskeleton, but as far as the pharynx-stomach-intestine tract is concerned, it remains on the outside, and the primordial annelid is still inside our body, which swallows, digests, discards, and excretes. We’re worms, after all. I look at the endoscope through its eye. We’re not so different."
